  bool increasingTriplet(vector<int>& nums) {
        
       if(nums.size()==1 || nums.size()==2)return false;
        
        int i = INT_MAX;
        int j = INT_MAX;
        
        for(auto x:nums){
            if(x<=i){
                i = x;    
            }
            else if(x<=j){
                j = x;
            }
            else
                return true;
        
        }
        return false;
        
        
    }


We only update the first and second position when a new no. is lesser than the first or a new no. is lesser than the second.

Then if a no. is found smaller than INT_MAX/greater than second then we simply return true;

Also we are traversing from left to right. 
So after every new update/Overwriting we are getting better and expecting even smaller number as the third number.
